1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:01,648
P/E.

2
00:00:01,848 --> 00:00:03,129
Price to Earnings.

3
00:00:03,329 --> 00:00:06,868
The most used, and most misused, number in the stock market.

4
00:00:07,068 --> 00:00:09,885
Let's build it from the accounts, line by line.

5
00:00:10,635 --> 00:00:12,833
Start at the profit and loss statement.

6
00:00:13,033 --> 00:00:15,551
Revenue at the top, one thousand crore.

7
00:00:15,751 --> 00:00:18,223
Minus costs, eight hundred and twenty.

8
00:00:18,423 --> 00:00:20,121
Minus interest, thirty.

9
00:00:20,321 --> 00:00:21,894
Minus tax, fifty.

10
00:00:22,094 --> 00:00:25,764
What is left at the bottom is net profit: one hundred crore.

11
00:00:26,514 --> 00:00:29,523
Divide that by the number of shares, ten crore shares,

12
00:00:29,523 --> 00:00:32,125
and you get earnings per share: ten rupees.

13
00:00:32,325 --> 00:00:33,438
That is the E.

14
00:00:34,188 --> 00:00:36,303
The P is just today's share price.

15
00:00:36,503 --> 00:00:38,168
Say two hundred rupees.

16
00:00:38,368 --> 00:00:42,529
So P/E is two hundred divided by ten, which is twenty.

17
00:00:43,279 --> 00:00:44,588
Read it like the shop.

18
00:00:44,788 --> 00:00:46,046
At a P/E of twenty,

19
00:00:46,046 --> 00:00:50,634
you are paying twenty rupees for every one rupee of yearly profit.

20
00:00:50,834 --> 00:00:51,998
If profits stayed flat,

21
00:00:51,998 --> 00:00:54,781
it would take twenty years to earn your money back.

22
00:00:54,981 --> 00:00:55,840
Flip it over:

23
00:00:55,840 --> 00:00:59,689
one divided by twenty is a five percent earnings yield.

24
00:00:59,889 --> 00:01:02,161
Now compare that with a fixed deposit.

25
00:01:02,911 --> 00:01:04,031
Three warnings.

26
00:01:04,231 --> 00:01:06,727
A high P/E is not always expensive:

27
00:01:06,727 --> 00:01:09,373
the market may expect fast growth.

28
00:01:09,573 --> 00:01:13,905
A low P/E is not always cheap: profits may be about to fall.

29
00:01:14,105 --> 00:01:17,519
And if there is no profit, there is no P/E at all.

30
00:01:17,719 --> 00:01:20,100
Always compare against the same industry,

31
00:01:20,100 --> 00:01:22,050
and the company's own history.

